Look at [Shadertoys.com](http://Shadertoys.com) there are a lot of demos to look at and inspect their code and logic, what techniques are being used. [https://iquilezles.org/articles/](https://iquilezles.org/articles/) also has a lot of great stuff on raymarching and SDF vectors.

Here's some water code from another app I was doing that looked really good, might help to pull apart:

     // OPTIMIZATION 1: Reduced FBM Octaves from 5 -> 3
            // The water is dark and moving; 5 octaves of detail is wasted calculation.
            float fbm(vec3 p) {
                float v = 0.0;
                float a = 0.5;
                for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
                    v += a * noise(p);
                    p *= 2.1;
                    a *= 0.48;
                }
                return v;
            }
